  "faces_total counts faces, not burns: a face is a FILE, and two files of one leg at two cutoffs are two rows",
  "names_in differs between the generations (1271 on the sweeps, 1317 on the twins) because the panel grew, so a neutralised COUNT is not comparable across generations -- the ladder intersection is",
  "the sweep generation carries no cutoff control, so its repair column sits beside a null refresh: that is a defect of the face, not a finding about the repair",
  "the repair channel is declared per row; a row whose count comes from counting non-zero delta rows is not the same measurement as a twin's pair.summary",
  "ladder_row_is_a_control is derived from the face's own neutralised set, cross-checked against the face's own claim where one exists, and left null where no census exists -- a contradiction is flagged, never resolved",
  "not_a_declared_twin is an annotation, not an indictment: the gap-limit and screen-registration faces census prints without being a twin of any runner",
  "ordering bands are conventions (1.25 / 0.8); the ratio column is published so a reader can re-band the table without re-burning it"
